"""`aspect ci bazelrc` — write a Bazel rc that configures vanilla `bazel` calls to
use Aspect's remote services and recommended optimizations.

`aspect <task>` injects its Bazel flags itself (see `feature/workflows.axl`,
`feature/deployment.axl`, and `lib/aspect_flags.axl`, the table of every flag
Aspect sets and why). A bare `bazel build` started from the same job gets none
of that. This command writes the equivalent where vanilla `bazel` will find it —
`~/.bazelrc` is the first user rc Bazel loads, picked up with no `--bazelrc`
plumbing:

  - On an Aspect Workflows runner, `~/.bazelrc` is written whole. The runner is
    ours, nothing else configures Bazel on it, and rewriting the file is what
    keeps it in step with the runner's environment. The runner's BES backend is
    written too, so vanilla `bazel` reaches the Web UI like a task does, and a
    runner that names a remote executor gets an opt-in `--config=aspect-exec`
    for it. Tasks themselves run with `--nohome_rc` and stream BES from the
    CLI, so nothing in this file reaches them. Bazel reads the home rc after the workspace rc, so a
    repository whose own rc names a different `--bes_backend` for vanilla calls
    keeps it by opting out: `--omit-bazel-flag=--bes_backend`.
  - Anywhere else, the rc goes to `~/.aspect/bazelrc` and `~/.bazelrc` gains
    one `try-import` line for it, so an rc another setup step or the developer
    wrote survives and re-running never accumulates anything. That rc is inert
    until a `--config=aspect-*` is named, but for the CI-host tuning
    (`aspect-ci`, `aspect-<ci host>`) and a cache or BES the `ASPECT_WORKFLOWS_*`
    env names where someone set those — so importing it into a developer's own
    rc changes nothing by itself.

It is the in-CLI successor to `rosetta bazelrc`: the CI integrations (the
setup-aspect GitHub Action, Buildkite plugin, CircleCI orb, GitLab component)
call this instead of `rosetta` once `rosetta` is gone from the runner image.

Every flag in the rc sits in a named `--config` group (`lib/rc_groups.axl`):
`aspect-ci` for CI-host tuning, `aspect-cache` and `aspect-bes` for what a cache
or a BES justifies, `aspect-<ci host>` for what the detected host needs
(`--color=yes` where Bazel misdetects), `aspect-runner` for the endpoints and
specifics the `ASPECT_WORKFLOWS_*` env names, and `aspect-exec` for the runner's
executor. The groups that apply here are enabled at the top with
`common --config=<group>` lines — on a Workflows runner that is most of them,
elsewhere only `aspect-ci`, the host's, and whatever the env names — and the
rest are opt-in by name, so `--announce_rc` says which group set every flag.
After them come the `--config=aspect-*` deployment sections from
`lib/deployment_rc.axl`, one per deployment `aspect auth status` knows, which
chain to the same groups. The credential helper those sections name is the
binary running this command — it certainly exists, whereas a bare `aspect` on
PATH may not for a later `bazel` step, and Bazel fails outright on a helper it
cannot find. Startup options have no `--config`, so the runner's output paths
are plain `startup` lines.

`--omit-bazel-flag` drops any tuning flag from the rc, inside whichever group
holds it (a group emptied that way disappears along with the lines that named
it); the endpoints, credentials, and runner paths in `PROTECTED_FLAGS` are refused. This is the rc's
own knob: tasks have `--bazel-flags:omit` (see `feature/bazel_flags.axl`), since
vanilla `bazel` and tasks may want different omissions.

How the rc renders and how the import line is placed live in
`lib/bazelrc_file.axl`. Version-gated flags are resolved against the detected
Bazel version (assumed-latest when undetectable) before writing. Only file
output is supported — there is no stdout mode.
"""

load(
    "./private/lib/aspect_flags.axl",
    "omit_flags",
    "protected_omissions",
    "runner_exec_log_path",
    "runner_startup_flags",
    "temp_exec_log_path",
    "written_flag_names",
)
load(
    "./private/lib/bazelrc_file.axl",
    "ImportAction",
    "RcConfig",
    "command_sections",
    "ensure_import",
    "import_line",
    "is_config_chain",
    "prune_configs",
    "render_bazelrc",
    "startup_flags_for_rc",
)
load("./private/lib/deployment_rc.axl", "SECTION_FLAG_NAMES", "config_collisions", "deployment_configs")
load("./private/lib/environment.axl", "bazel_misdetects_color", "get_workflows_environment", "info", "is_aspect_workflows_runner")
load("./private/lib/rc_groups.axl", "enabled_groups", "exec_group", "host_group", "runner_group", "tuning_groups")

# Where the rc lives under the home directory, and the user rc that imports it.
_GENERATED_RC = ".aspect/bazelrc"
_USER_RC = ".bazelrc"

_IMPORT_VERBS = {
    ImportAction("created"): "created %s with it",
    ImportAction("unchanged"): "%s already imports it",
    ImportAction("appended"): "added the import to %s",
    ImportAction("replaced"): "replaced the lines this command had generated in %s with the import",
}

def _home_path(ctx: TaskContext, relative: str) -> str:
    """`~/<relative>`; ends the task when the home directory can't be resolved."""
    home = ctx.std.env.home_dir()
    if home == None:
        ctx.std.process.exit(1, "Could not resolve your home directory to default the rc paths. Pass --output=<path> (and --import-into=<rc>) explicitly.")
    return home.rstrip("/") + "/" + relative

def _write(ctx: TaskContext, path: str, content: str) -> None:
    """Write `content` to `path`, creating parent directories."""
    parent = path.rstrip("/").rsplit("/", 1)
    if len(parent) == 2 and parent[0] and not ctx.std.fs.exists(parent[0]):
        ctx.std.fs.create_dir_all(parent[0])
    ctx.std.fs.write(path, content)

def _resolve(ctx: TaskContext, flags: list, bazel_version: str | None) -> list:
    """Resolve the version-gated `(flag, constraint)` tuples in `flags` against the
    detected Bazel version via the bazelrc runtime: a blank RunCommand whose
    `common` bucket holds every flag, expanded assumed-latest when the version is
    unknown. Config chain entries are kept verbatim ahead of the rest — the blank
    RunCommand has no section for them to expand into."""
    chain = [f for f in flags if is_config_chain(f)]
    rest = [f for f in flags if not is_config_chain(f)]
    rc = ctx.bazel.new_rc(flags = rest, version = bazel_version)
    return chain + rc.expand(command = "common")

def _groups(ctx: TaskContext, environment, on_runner: bool) -> list:
    """Every group `rc_groups.axl` defines for this host, in the order written:
    the tuning groups, the CI host's, the runner's, and the runner's executor.
    The BES group's execution log goes under the runner's job tmpdir on a
    runner and under the temp dir elsewhere."""
    exec_log_path = runner_exec_log_path(environment) if on_runner else temp_exec_log_path(ctx.std, ctx.task.id)
    return (
        tuning_groups(exec_log_path) +
        host_group(environment, bazel_misdetects_color(ctx.std.env)) +
        runner_group(environment, on_runner) +
        exec_group(environment)
    )

def _sections(ctx: TaskContext) -> list:
    """The `--config` sections for this machine's deployments. Reads
    `deployments()`, not `list()`: nothing here needs login status, and a CI
    runner may have no credential store to read. The credential helper they
    name is the binary running this command."""
    return deployment_configs(ctx.aspect.auth.deployments(), ctx.std.env.current_exe())

def _bazelrc_impl(ctx: TaskContext) -> int | TaskConclusion:
    omitted = ctx.args.omit_bazel_flags
    blocked = protected_omissions(omitted)
    if blocked:
        return TaskConclusion(exit_code = 1, message = "--omit-bazel-flag cannot drop %s: endpoints, credentials, and the runner's paths are what make the build Aspect's." % ", ".join(blocked))

    environment = get_workflows_environment(ctx.std)
    on_runner = is_aspect_workflows_runner(ctx.std.env)
    startup_flags = []
    if on_runner:
        if environment.runner == None:
            return TaskConclusion(exit_code = 1, message = "Running on an Aspect Workflows runner but the runner metadata env vars are missing, so the cache flags cannot be generated. This usually means an older runner image; upgrade the runner.")
        startup_flags = startup_flags_for_rc(runner_startup_flags(environment, ctx.std.env.aspect_root_dir()))

    groups = _groups(ctx, environment, on_runner)
    configs = groups + _sections(ctx)
    collisions = config_collisions(configs)
    if collisions:
        return TaskConclusion(exit_code = 1, message = "\n".join(collisions))

    bazel_version = ctx.bazel.version()
    startup_flags = omit_flags(startup_flags, omitted)
    configs = [
        RcConfig(name = c.name, source = c.source, comment = c.comment, flags = _resolve(ctx, omit_flags(c.flags, omitted), bazel_version))
        for c in configs
    ]
    (configs, enabled) = prune_configs(configs, enabled_groups(environment, groups))

    # A runner's user rc is written whole; elsewhere the rc is a separate file
    # the user rc imports.
    output = ctx.args.output or _home_path(ctx, _USER_RC if on_runner else _GENERATED_RC)
    _write(ctx, output, render_bazelrc(startup_flags, enabled, command_sections(bazel_version), configs))

    optional = [c.name for c in configs if c.name not in enabled]
    summary = "Wrote Aspect bazelrc to %s: enabled --config groups %s; opt-in %s" % (output, ", ".join(enabled), ", ".join(optional))
    if len(optional) == len(groups) - len(enabled):
        summary += " (no deployment advertises endpoints here; see `aspect auth status`, and `aspect auth login` records Aspect Cloud's)"

    user_rc = ctx.args.import_into or _home_path(ctx, _USER_RC)
    if user_rc == output:
        info(ctx.std, summary + ".")
        return 0

    existing = ctx.std.fs.read_to_string(user_rc) if ctx.std.fs.exists(user_rc) else None
    result = ensure_import(existing, import_line(output), written_flag_names() + SECTION_FLAG_NAMES)
    if result.action != ImportAction("unchanged"):
        _write(ctx, user_rc, result.content)
    info(ctx.std, summary + "; " + _IMPORT_VERBS[result.action] % user_rc + ".")
    return 0

bazelrc = task(
    group = ["ci"],
    summary = "Write a Bazel rc that points vanilla `bazel` calls at Aspect's remote services and recommended optimizations.",
    description = "Write a Bazel rc so vanilla `bazel` calls pick up the same configuration that `aspect <task>` injects. On an Aspect Workflows runner `~/.bazelrc` is written whole; elsewhere the rc goes to `~/.aspect/bazelrc` and `~/.bazelrc` gains a single `try-import` line for it, added once. Every flag sits in a named `--config` group — `aspect-ci`, `aspect-cache`, `aspect-bes`, `aspect-<ci host>`, `aspect-runner`, `aspect-exec` — and the groups that apply on this host are enabled at the top of the file (`bazel build --announce_rc` shows which group set what). On a Workflows runner that is the recommended CI/profiling flags plus its remote cache, BES, repository cache, and per-runner output paths, with `--config=aspect-exec` opting into its remote executor; elsewhere the deployment sections are opt-in: `--config=aspect-cloud` for Aspect Cloud's remote cache + BES, `--config=aspect-<name>` for a configured deployment (`aspect auth status`), `--config=aspect-<name>-exec` to add its remote execution, and `--config=aspect` for the default deployment — authenticated through the `aspect get` credential helper.",
    implementation = _bazelrc_impl,
    args = {
        "output": args.string(
            default = "",
            description = "Rc file to write, rewritten on every run. Defaults to `~/.bazelrc` on an Aspect Workflows runner and to `~/.aspect/bazelrc` elsewhere. Parent directories are created if needed. Only file output is supported — there is no stdout mode.",
        ),
        "import_into": args.string(
            long = "import-into",
            default = "",
            description = "User rc that receives a `try-import <output>` line, added only when not already present. Defaults to `~/.bazelrc`; on an Aspect Workflows runner the output is `~/.bazelrc` itself and no import is needed.",
        ),
        "omit_bazel_flags": args.string_list(
            long = "omit-bazel-flag",
            description = "A Bazel flag this rc would otherwise set that you do not want, named as Aspect spells it (e.g. --omit-bazel-flag=--heap_dump_on_oom; a value after `=` is ignored). Repeat for several. Set it once per repo in config.axl via ctx.tasks[\"bazelrc\"].args.omit_bazel_flags. Endpoints, credentials, and the runner's output paths cannot be omitted. Tasks have their own knob, --bazel-flags:omit.",
        ),
    },
)
